T*
('report-sample' 'unsafe-inline' https:;) Tj
T*
(    ```) Tj
T*
(*   **Risk Explanation:** The use of `'unsafe-inline'` allows JavaScript to be executed directly ) Tj
T*
(within HTML without sanitization, bypassing standard script context protections. While the presence ) Tj
T*
(of `upgrade-insecure-requests` and `base-uri 'self'` provides some defense in depth, retaining ) Tj
T*
(inline scripts significantly increases the attack surface for XSS if a new vulnerability is ) Tj
T*
(introduced or misconfigured content is served.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(### B. Missing Referrer-Policy \(Low Severity\)) Tj
T*
(*   **Issue:** The response headers do not include a `Referrer-Policy`.) Tj
T*
(*   **Risk Explanation:** Without this header, browsers may send full URI referrers by default to ) Tj
T*
(cross-origin requests. This can expose sensitive information such as user session IDs or internal ) Tj
T*
(paths in server logs and analytics tools \(e.g., Google Analytics\), aiding privacy violations and ) Tj
