T*
() Tj
T*
(## 11. Overall Conclusion) Tj
T*
(The `https://www.hackerone.com/` domain demonstrates a generally secure posture with HTTPS ) Tj
T*
(enforcement, HSTS, and X-Frame-Protection enabled via Cloudflare. However, the **Medium severity ) Tj
T*
(finding regarding the Content-Security-Policy** is the most significant risk identified. The ) Tj
T*
(presence of `'unsafe-inline'` and `'unsafe-eval'` creates an unnecessary trust boundary that could ) Tj
T*
(be exploited to execute arbitrary code if a vulnerability exists in the content rendering engine ) Tj
T*
(\(e.g., Drupal\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Immediate remediation involves tightening the CSP policy by removing permissive directives. While ) Tj
T*
(SQL Injection was not tested due to lack of input parameters, this is a procedural limitation rather) Tj
T*
( than a security flaw; manual testing remains necessary for comprehensive coverage. The missing ) Tj
T*
(Referrer and Permissions headers represent minor privacy risks that should be addressed in future ) Tj
T*
(hardening cycles.) Tj
T*
() Tj
